  - question: How much does fascia repair cost in Huntsville?
    answer: "<p>Fascia repair typically costs $5-15 per linear foot in Huntsville, depending on the extent of damage, wood type, and accessibility. Most homes need 10-40 feet of fascia replaced. We'll provide an exact quote after inspecting your specific situation — there are no surprises when the bill comes.</p>"
  - question: How do I know if my fascia is rotted?
    answer: "<p>Signs of fascia damage include: paint peeling or bubbling, soft or spongy wood when pressed, visible dark staining or discoloration, gutters pulling away from the house, or gaps between fascia and soffit. We inspect fascia as part of every gutter estimate — many homeowners don't know they have damage until we point it out.</p>"
  - question: Can you repair fascia without replacing gutters?
    answer: "<p>Yes! If your gutters are in good condition, we can carefully remove them, repair the fascia underneath, and reinstall. However, this often costs nearly as much as new gutters since we're handling them twice. It may make sense to upgrade while we're already doing the work.</p>"
  - question: What causes fascia to rot in Huntsville?
